1
00:00:03,350 --> 00:00:05,800
Last step: make the project easy to show.

2
00:00:06,080 --> 00:00:11,747
A README that explains it, live docs, a green build badge, and a warehouse anyone can query.

3
00:00:12,697 --> 00:00:16,280
On GitHub, open the repository's Settings, then Pages.

4
00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:20,934
Under Source, choose GitHub Actions, so our workflow can publish the docs.

5
00:00:21,884 --> 00:00:31,101
In Studio, open the workflow file, and paste three more build steps at the end: generate the docs, copy the site files, and upload them for Pages.

6
00:00:32,051 --> 00:00:36,174
And a second job, docs, that runs after build and deploys the site.

7
00:00:36,454 --> 00:00:37,053
Save.

8
00:00:38,003 --> 00:00:38,985
Now the README.

9
00:00:39,265 --> 00:00:48,931
Open it, select all, and paste the new one: a build badge, a docs link, what the project does and where to look, how to query the warehouse, and how to run it yourself.

10
00:00:49,211 --> 00:00:49,811
Save.

11
00:00:50,761 --> 00:00:55,197
Git tab: stage all, type a message, publish docs and README, and commit.

12
00:01:03,593 --> 00:01:04,568
Sync Changes.

13
00:01:04,848 --> 00:01:06,246
The push starts the workflow.

14
00:01:08,693 --> 00:01:13,573
On GitHub, the Actions tab shows the run, now with two jobs: build, then docs.

15
00:01:14,523 --> 00:01:16,191
A minute later, both are green.

16
00:01:17,723 --> 00:01:23,288
The docs are live on GitHub Pages, for anyone, with the lineage graph of the whole project.

17
00:01:24,238 --> 00:01:28,253
And the repository page shows the README, with the green build badge.

18
00:01:29,203 --> 00:01:31,060
And anyone can query the warehouse.

19
00:01:31,340 --> 00:01:38,151
With DuckDB, attach prod dot duckdb straight from the GitHub release, read only, and select from the marts.

20
00:01:39,101 --> 00:01:45,920
East Harlem North leads, with a hundred forty-three thousand trips: built by CI, and read over the internet.

21
00:01:46,870 --> 00:01:48,047
That's Project 1.

22
00:01:48,327 --> 00:01:59,323
Raw files and a seed, models with ref, descriptions, docs and the DAG, tables where they matter, tests, CI on every push, live docs, and a warehouse anyone can query.

23
00:01:59,603 --> 00:02:03,123
All built in Rosetta DBT Studio, and all on GitHub.
